[b]A mod for Mount & Blade II: Bannerlord.[/b]

Made by two of us: the code and all technical work by Claude (Opus 5.5), an AI; the idea, feedback and playtesting by [url=https://github.com/TraxData313]Trax[/url], Bible believer and engineer in AI/ML/Python/Applied Maths.

Change the gear of your own troops.

Open any troop in the [b]Encyclopedia[/b] - say the Battanian Volunteer - press [b]Edit gear[/b] and swap his weapons, armour or horse slot by slot. Only troops of [b]your[/b] parties wear your version: your party, your clan's parties and your garrisons. Everyone else in Calradia keeps the vanilla gear.
[list]
[*]A troop has several vanilla gear sets. Edit each set on its own, or press [b]All sets[/b] on a slot to put that item on every set.
[*][b]Reset[/b] one slot, [b]Reset this set[/b], or [b]Reset whole unit to vanilla[/b].
[*]The item picker shows each item's tier and price, and filters by tier, culture and type, or by name.
[*]On the Encyclopedia page of an edited troop, switch between [b]Vanilla[/b] and [b]My version[/b].
[*]The party screen shows your troops in their new gear.
[*]Edits are free and instant, anywhere on the map.
[*]Works with [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3674824323]Troop Equipment Upgrade[/url]: it still sees the vanilla troop and prices upgrades as before.
[/list]

[h1]Good to know[/h1]
[list]
[*]Not for troops that another mod rewrites (My Little Warband and the like).
[*]Gear counts in battles you fight. Auto-resolve does not look at gear.
[*]Formations stay as they are: a spearman you give a bow or a horse still lines up as infantry.
[*]Heroes, prisoners, tournaments and the arena stay vanilla.
[/list]

[h1]Requirements[/h1]
[list]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2859188632]Harmony[/url]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2859222409]UIExtenderEx[/url]
[/list]
Works with or without War Sails. For Bannerlord v1.4.8. Safe to add or remove mid-campaign.

The idea of an in-game gear editor comes from My Little Warband. This mod is written from scratch and uses none of its code or files.

Free and open — public domain (The Unlicense). Do whatever you like with it.
To thank me, open [url=https://github.com/TraxData313]my GitHub profile[/url] and read my top pinned.

Not on Steam? Download it from the [url=https://github.com/TraxData313/my-troops-gear/releases/latest]GitHub Releases page[/url]. Source code and README: [url=https://github.com/TraxData313/my-troops-gear]github.com/TraxData313/my-troops-gear[/url]
